Feature: Visual Comparison tests for bar chart

    Background:
        Given "Factor Based Analysis" with default settings is added to a report for portfolio "SNP100" with date "20230202"

    Scenario: Validate FBA bar chart with combo settings (chart type and secondary axis settings)
        When I right click on "SNP100" cell to open context menu, hover on "Open Chart", then click on "Bar chart"
        # Remove the FBA widget so that it does not appear in the snapshot testing for the FBA bar chart.
        And I delete "Factor Based Analysis" widget
        And I maximize "Bar chart" widget
        Then "Bar chart" should be displayed, aligning with the snapshot "fbaBarChart_SNP100"

        When I open widget settings modal from "Bar chart"
        And I click format tab
        And I click secondary axis checkbox for column "2" (CHECK)
        And I apply widget settings
        Then "Bar chart" should be displayed, aligning with the snapshot "fbaBarChart_SNP100_with_secondary_axis"

        When I open widget settings modal from "Bar chart"
        And I click format tab
        And I select chart type "Marker" for column "2"
        And I apply widget settings
        Then "Bar chart" should be displayed, aligning with the snapshot "fbaBarChart_SNP100_with_marker_and_secondary_axis"
